WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:10.680
So element ununpentium, that’s the element
115, is in the same group of

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:19.660
the periodic table as nitrogen, phosphorus,
antimony, and arsenic, and

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:27.590
so we can, even without knowing or seeing
a real sample, we can tell

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:33.109
quite a lot about what the chemistry might
be like. This is, after all, what

00:00:33.109 --> 00:00:36.940
Mendeleev’s triumph with the periodic table
was, that he looked at where

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:40.579
there were holes in the periodic table where
he reckoned there should be

00:00:40.579 --> 00:00:47.359
elements and he predicted their properties
so that we can tell that this

00:00:47.359 --> 00:00:58.909
element, Uup, is going to be in some ways
like the elements in the Group

00:00:58.909 --> 00:01:04.299
15. Group 15 here, if you can look, is the
one that is nitrogen,

00:01:04.299 --> 00:01:11.420
phosphorous, arsenic, antimony and bismuth,
and it will be down here. Until

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:17.380
recently I used to lecture on Group 15 and
I mentioned when this Uup

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:21.140
had been discovered I set a little exam question
and asked the students

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:25.439
which group it would be in, thinking that
they would have to count it, and

00:01:25.439 --> 00:01:29.931
not realising that the exam paper had a periodic
table with it marked in

00:01:29.931 --> 00:01:32.639
the right place, so they got some marks for
free.

